{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg936\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\froman\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset134 \'cb\'ce\'cc\'e5;}{\f2\fnil\fcharset134 \'ba\'da\'cc\'e5;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\lang2052\f1\fs24 \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs36\sa70\qc \b \'c9\'cf\'ba\'a3\'ca\'d0\'d0\'a1\'d1\'a7\'c8\'fd\'c4\'ea\'bc\'b6\'d3\'a2\'d3\'ef\'d7\'db\'ba\'cf\'b8\'b4\'cf\'b0\'be\'ed\'a3\'a8\'c8\'fd\'a3\'a9\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs25\sa70\qc \'bb\'a6\'bd\'cc\'b0\'e6\'c8\'fd\'c4\'ea\'bc\'b6\'c9\'cf\'cf\'c2\'b2\'e1\'d7\'db\'ba\'cf\'d5\'ef\'b6\'cf \'a1\'a4 \'cb\'c4\'c4\'ea\'bc\'b6\'bf\'aa\'d1\'a7\'c7\'b0\'c7\'bf\'bb\'af\'a3\'a82026\'c4\'ea9\'d4\'c2\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs23\sa100\qc School: ____________    Class: ____________    Name: ____________    Date: ____________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b I. Sounds and letters\'a3\'a8A\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baRead and judge. Write S or D.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. cake \'a1\'aa cat\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. he \'a1\'aa she\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. bike \'a1\'aa kite\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. dog \'a1\'aa nose\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. duck \'a1\'aa bus\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. pen \'a1\'aa red\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 7. name \'a1\'aa rain\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 8. sun \'a1\'aa pupil\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b I. Sounds and letters\'a3\'a8B\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baCircle the word with a different vowel sound.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. A. cake\'a1\'a1B. bag\'a1\'a1C. name\'a1\'a1D. rain\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. A. he\'a1\'a1B. me\'a1\'a1C. pen\'a1\'a1D. she\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. A. bike\'a1\'a1B. kite\'a1\'a1C. fish\'a1\'a1D. nine\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. A. dog\'a1\'a1B. box\'a1\'a1C. nose\'a1\'a1D. hot\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. A. sun\'a1\'a1B. duck\'a1\'a1C. bus\'a1\'a1D. pupil\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b I. Sounds and letters\'a3\'a8C\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baLetters and time\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. Write the missing small letters in alphabetical order:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql B\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a1D\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a1F\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a1H\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a1J\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a1L\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a1N\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a1P\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a1R\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a1T\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a1V\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a1X\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a1Z\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. Write the times in English:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6:30 ________\'a1\'a17:15 ________\'a1\'a19:45 ________\'a1\'a112:00 ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b II. Vocabulary\'a3\'a8A\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baChoose the odd one out.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. A. juice\'a1\'a1B. milk\'a1\'a1C. bread\'a1\'a1D. water\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. A. cloudy\'a1\'a1B. scarf\'a1\'a1C. gloves\'a1\'a1D. sweater\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. A. uncle\'a1\'a1B. aunt\'a1\'a1C. teacher\'a1\'a1D. cousin\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. A. library\'a1\'a1B. museum\'a1\'a1C. dinner\'a1\'a1D. park\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. A. autumn\'a1\'a1B. cloudy\'a1\'a1C. spring\'a1\'a1D. summer\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. A. plane\'a1\'a1B. elephant\'a1\'a1C. bear\'a1\'a1D. panda\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 7. A. eye\'a1\'a1B. gloves\'a1\'a1C. ear\'a1\'a1D. nose\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 8. A. breakfast\'a1\'a1B. bread\'a1\'a1C. lunch\'a1\'a1D. dinner\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b II. Vocabulary\'a3\'a8B\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baRead the riddles and write the words.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. It is cold. You wear it around your neck in winter. It is a s________.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. You wear them on your hands when it is cold. They are g________.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. It is the first meal of a day. It is b________.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. It comes after Thursday. It is F________.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. It is very big and grey. It has a long nose. It is an e________.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. It comes after summer. It is a________.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 7. You have many of them in your mouth. They are t________.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 8. It can fly in the sky and takes people far away. It is a p________.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b II. Vocabulary\'a3\'a8C\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baComplete the words with the missing letters.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. br__kfast\'a3\'a8\'d4\'e7\'b2\'cd\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. fav__rite\'a3\'a8\'d7\'ee\'cf\'b2\'bb\'b6\'b5\'c4\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. v__etable\'a3\'a8\'ca\'df\'b2\'cb\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. be__tiful\'a3\'a8\'c3\'c0\'c0\'f6\'b5\'c4\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. grandm__ther\'a3\'a8\'c4\'cc\'c4\'cc/\'cd\'e2\'c6\'c5\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. w__ther\'a3\'a8\'cc\'ec\'c6\'f8\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 7. elep__nt\'a3\'a8\'b4\'f3\'cf\'f3\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 8. Th__sday\'a3\'a8\'d0\'c7\'c6\'da\'cb\'c4\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b II. Vocabulary\'a3\'a8D\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baChoose and write. Use each word only once.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. between\'a1\'a1cloudy\'a1\'a1thirsty\'a1\'a1umbrella\'a1\'a1grandparents\'a1\'a1favourite\'a1\'a1winter\'a1\'a1write\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. What is your\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9colour?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. It is\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9today. Take an umbrella.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. We have a rest\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9two lessons.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. I drink some water because I am\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. My\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9live with us.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 7. I can\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9a letter in English.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 8. It is cold and snowy in\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 9. It is raining. Take your\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b II. Vocabulary\'a3\'a8E\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baWrite the English words.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. \'d0\'c7\'c6\'da\'cb\'c4 ________\'a1\'a12. \'c7\'ef\'cc\'ec ________\'a1\'a13. \'c3\'ab\'d2\'c2 ________\'a1\'a14. \'bc\'d0\'bf\'cb\'c9\'c0 ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. \'c1\'ac\'d2\'c2\'c8\'b9 ________\'a1\'a16. \'d4\'e7\'b2\'cd ________\'a1\'a17. \'d7\'ee\'cf\'b2\'bb\'b6\'b5\'c4 ________\'a1\'a18. \'d2\'f5\'d3\'ea\'b5\'c4 ________\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b III. Grammar\'a3\'a8A\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baFind one mistake in each sentence and write the correct sentence.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. She go to school by bus.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. There is two oranges in the box.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. What is you doing?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. My brother don't like coffee.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. These are my glove.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. How much books are there?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 7. It is rain today. Take an umbrella.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 8. He can swims in the river.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 9. Is this you pen?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 10. I get up on seven o'clock.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b III. Grammar\'a3\'a8B\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baChoose the correct word.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. I have a cat. (It / Its) name is Mimi. I like (it / its) very much.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. That is Alice. (She / Her) is my classmate. (She / Her) hair is long.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. The boys are my friends. (They / Their) are in Class Two. (They / Their) teacher is Miss Li.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. This is (we / our) new classroom. (We / Our) like it very much.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. Are these (you / your) shoes? Yes, (they / their) are.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b III. Grammar\'a3\'a8C\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baFill in do, does, don't, doesn't, is, are or am.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. My sister\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9like coffee.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9your father a firefighter?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9you have any brothers?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. The children\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9playing in the playground.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. I\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9like juice. I like water.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. What\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9your mother do?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 7. Kitty and I\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9good friends.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 8. Look! This\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9my new pencil case.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b III. Grammar\'a3\'a8D\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baMake sentences. Put the words in the correct order.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. today / How / the / weather / is / ?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. have / I / breakfast / at / seven / half / past / .\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. Whose / scarf / this / is / ?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. my / is / This / new / favourite / sweater / .\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. My / likes / brother / elephants / big / .\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. there / books / any / bag / in / your / Are / ?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 7. can / Danny / fly / kite / his / .\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 8. like / you / Would / some / juice / ?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b III. Grammar\'a3\'a8E\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baWrite a question for each answer.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. ? \'a1\'aa\'a1\'aa I get up at seven.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. ? \'a1\'aa\'a1\'aa My uncle is a policeman.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. ? \'a1\'aa\'a1\'aa There are four seasons in a year.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. ? \'a1\'aa\'a1\'aa The gloves are Kitty's.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. ? \'a1\'aa\'a1\'aa Yes, I like spring.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. ? \'a1\'aa\'a1\'aa No, she cannot swim.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b IV. Language use\'a3\'a8A\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baComplete the dialogue. Choose the correct sentences.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. A. Can I help you?\'a1\'a1B. Which one do you like?\'a1\'a1C. May I try it on?\'a1\'a1D. It is too small.\'a1\'a1E. How much is it?\'a1\'a1F. I need a new coat.\'a1\'a1G. Thank you.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. Shop assistant: Good morning! 1.\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. Jill: Yes. 2.\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. Shop assistant: Here are the coats. 3.\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. Jill: I like the red one. 4.\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. Shop assistant: Sure. Here you are.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 7. Jill: Hmm. 5.\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9Have you got a bigger one?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 8. Shop assistant: How about this blue one?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 9. Jill: It fits me well. 6.\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 10. Shop assistant: It is ninety yuan.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 11. Jill: OK. I'll take it. 7.\'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b IV. Language use\'a3\'a8B\'a3\'a9\'a3\'baPut the dialogue in the correct order. Write 1 to 6.\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9How much is this birthday card?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9Here you are.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9Yes, please. I want a birthday card for my mother.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9It is six yuan.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9Can I help you?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9OK. I'll take it. Thank you.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b V. Reading A \'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'d2\'bb\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql Read the email. Judge with T or F. Dear Lucy, Thank you for your email. I am happy to be your penfriend. Let me tell you about my week. From Monday to Friday, I get up at half past six. I walk to school at seven. Lessons start at eight. On Monday I have Chinese, Maths, English and PE. On Tuesday I have Science. I like Science because we can do experiments. On Wednesday I have Art and Music. On Thursday I have Maths, Chinese, Science and Music. I go to the library on Friday afternoon. At weekends, I play football with my father on Saturday morning and visit my grandmother on Sunday. Please write to me about your week. Love, Tom\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9Tom gets up at six thirty on school days.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9He goes to school by bus.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9Lessons begin at eight o'clock.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9He has Science on Tuesday and Thursday.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9He goes to the library on Friday afternoon.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9He visits his grandmother on Saturday.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 7. \'a3\'a8\'a1\'a1\'a3\'a9This email is from Lucy to Tom.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b V. Reading B \'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'b6\'fe\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql Read the timetable and answer the questions. Monday: Chinese, Maths, Art, PE Tuesday: English, Chinese, Music, Science Wednesday: Maths, English, PE, Art Thursday: Chinese, Maths, Science, Music Friday: English, Chinese, Maths, Class Meeting\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. How many lessons are there every day?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. On which two days does Jack have PE?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. Does Jack have Art on Friday?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. Which subject does Jack have every school day?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. How many English lessons does Jack have in a week?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. On which two days can Jack do Science experiments?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b V. Reading C \'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'c8\'fd\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql Read the price list and answer the questions.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql Happy Clothes Shop (Sunday Sale)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql Sweater: 50 yuan (red / blue)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql T-shirt: 30 yuan (white / green)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql Coat: 120 yuan (black / purple)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql Scarf: 25 yuan (yellow / pink)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql Dress: 80 yuan (blue / white)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql Shorts: 40 yuan (grey / brown)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. Which is the cheapest? Which is the most expensive?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. Which is cheaper, a sweater or a dress?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. Alice has 80 yuan. Can she buy a sweater and a scarf? How much does she get back?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. Bob buys a T-shirt and a pair of shorts. How much does he pay?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. Kitty has 100 yuan. She buys a dress. How much money does she have left?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b V. Reading D \'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'cb\'c4\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql Read the zoo poster. Answer the questions.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql Animal Day at City Zoo\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql 10:00 \'a1\'aa Elephant show\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql 11:30 \'a1\'aa Lunch time\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql 13:00 \'a1\'aa Monkey show\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql 14:30 \'a1\'aa Bird show\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql 16:00 \'a1\'aa Panda feeding\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa120\ql Rules: Don't feed the animals. Don't shout. Stay with your parents.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. When is the monkey show?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. What time can children watch the pandas eat?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 3. It is 11:45. Is it lunch time or show time?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 4. Can visitors give sandwiches to the elephants? Why or why not?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 5. Kitty arrives at the zoo at 9:30. She wants to see the elephant show. How long does she wait?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 6. After the bird show, what can children do at 15:20 according to the poster?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs27\sa90\sb180\ql \b VI. Writing \'d0\'b4\'d7\'f7\'a3\'a8\'c8\'ce\'d1\'a1\'d2\'bb\'cc\'e2\'a3\'a9\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 1. Write an email to your new penfriend in about five sentences. Tell him or her your name, your age, your school subject, what you can do and what you like.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa110\ql 2. My favourite season\'a3\'ba\'d3\'c35\'a1\'ab7\'be\'e4\'bb\'b0\'bd\'e9\'c9\'dc\'c4\'e3\'d7\'ee\'cf\'b2\'bb\'b6\'b5\'c4\'bc\'be\'bd\'da\'a3\'ac\'bf\'c9\'d2\'d4\'d0\'b4\'cc\'ec\'c6\'f8\'a1\'a2\'b4\'a9\'d7\'c5\'a1\'a2\'ca\'b3\'ce\'ef\'ba\'cd\'bb\'ee\'b6\'af\'a1\'a3\'d7\'a2\'d2\'e2\'be\'e4\'d7\'d3\'cd\'a8\'cb\'b3\'a3\'ac\'b4\'f3\'d0\'a1\'d0\'b4\'ba\'cd\'b1\'ea\'b5\'e3\'d5\'fd\'c8\'b7\'a1\'a3\par \page \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs30\sa100\qc \b \'b2\'ce\'bf\'bc\'b4\'f0\'b0\'b8\'a3\'a8\'b9\'a9\'bc\'d2\'b3\'a4\'ba\'cb\'b6\'d4\'a3\'a9\b0 \par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql I. Sounds and letters:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql S/D: 1. D\'a1\'a12. S\'a1\'a13. S\'a1\'a14. D\'a1\'a15. S\'a1\'a16. S\'a1\'a17. S\'a1\'a18. D\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Odd one out: 1. B\'a1\'a12. C\'a1\'a13. C\'a1\'a14. C\'a1\'a15. D\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Missing letters: b, d, f, h, j, l, n, p, r, t, v, x, z\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Times: 6:30 half past six\'a3\'bb7:15 a quarter past seven\'a3\'bb9:45 a quarter to ten\'a3\'bb12:00 twelve o'clock\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql II. Vocabulary:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Odd one out: 1. C\'a1\'a12. A\'a1\'a13. C\'a1\'a14. C\'a1\'a15. B\'a1\'a16. A\'a1\'a17. B\'a1\'a18. B\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Riddles: 1. scarf\'a1\'a12. gloves\'a1\'a13. breakfast\'a1\'a14. Friday\'a1\'a15. elephant\'a1\'a16. autumn\'a1\'a17. teeth\'a1\'a18. plane\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Missing letters: 1. ea\'a3\'a8breakfast\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a12. ou\'a3\'a8favourite\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a13. ge\'a3\'a8vegetable\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a14. au\'a3\'a8beautiful\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a15. o\'a3\'a8grandmother\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a16. ea\'a3\'a8weather\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a17. ha\'a3\'a8elephant\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a18. ur\'a3\'a8Thursday\'a3\'a9\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Choose and write: 1. favourite\'a1\'a12. cloudy\'a1\'a13. between\'a1\'a14. thirsty\'a1\'a15. grandparents\'a1\'a16. write\'a1\'a17. winter\'a1\'a18. umbrella\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Write English: 1. Thursday\'a1\'a12. autumn\'a1\'a13. sweater\'a1\'a14. jacket\'a1\'a15. dress\'a1\'a16. breakfast\'a1\'a17. favourite\'a1\'a18. rainy\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql III. Grammar and sentences:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Error hunt:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 1. She goes to school by bus.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 2. There are two oranges in the box.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 3. What are you doing?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 4. My brother doesn't like coffee.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 5. These are my gloves.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 6. How many books are there?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 7. It is rainy today. Take an umbrella.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 8. He can swim in the river.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 9. Is this your pen?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 10. I get up at seven o'clock.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Pronouns: 1. Its; it\'a1\'a12. She; Her\'a1\'a13. They; Their\'a1\'a14. our; We\'a1\'a15. your; they\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql do/does/be: 1. doesn't\'a1\'a12. Is\'a1\'a13. Do\'a1\'a14. are\'a1\'a15. don't\'a1\'a16. does\'a1\'a17. are\'a1\'a18. is\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Reorder:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 1. How is the weather today?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 2. I have breakfast at half past seven.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 3. Whose scarf is this?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 4. This is my new favourite sweater.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 5. My brother likes big elephants.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 6. Are there any books in your bag?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 7. Danny can fly his kite.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 8. Would you like some juice?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Questions for answers:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 1. What time do you get up?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 2. What does your uncle do?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 3. How many seasons are there in a year?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 4. Whose gloves are these?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 5. Do you like spring?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 6. Can she swim?\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql IV. Language use:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Clothes shop: 1. A\'a1\'a12. F\'a1\'a13. B\'a1\'a14. C\'a1\'a15. D\'a1\'a16. E\'a1\'a17. G\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Dialogue order: 1. Can I help you? 2. Yes, please. I want a birthday card for my mother. 3. How much is this birthday card? 4. It is six yuan. 5. OK. I'll take it. Thank you. 6. Here you are.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql V. Reading A:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 1. T\'a1\'a12. F\'a1\'a13. T\'a1\'a14. T\'a1\'a15. T\'a1\'a16. F\'a1\'a17. F\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql V. Reading B:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 1. There are four lessons every day.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 2. On Monday and Wednesday.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 3. No, he does not.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 4. Chinese.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 5. Three (on Tuesday, Wednesday and Friday).\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 6. On Tuesday and Thursday.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql V. Reading C:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 1. The scarf is the cheapest. The coat is the most expensive.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 2. A sweater is cheaper. (A sweater is 50 yuan; a dress is 80 yuan.)\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 3. Yes, she can. 50 + 25 = 75. She gets 80 - 75 = 5 yuan back.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 4. 30 + 40 = 70 yuan.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 5. 100 - 80 = 20 yuan.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql V. Reading D:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 1. At 13:00 (one o'clock in the afternoon).\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 2. At 16:00.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 3. It is lunch time.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 4. No, they cannot. The poster says, \'a1\'b0Don't feed the animals.\'a1\'b1\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 5. From 9:30 to 10:00 is 30 minutes.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql 6. The bird show is at 14:30. There is no activity at 15:20 in the poster, so children can wait for the panda feeding at 16:00 or follow their parents.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql VI. Writing:\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql Sample: My name is May. I am nine. I study at Sunny Primary School. I like English and Art. I can draw and ride a bike. I like pandas very much.\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs24\sa70\ql \'d0\'b4\'d7\'f7\'c6\'c0\'d4\'c4\'d6\'d8\'b5\'e3\'a3\'ba\'d6\'f7\'cc\'e2\'ca\'c7\'b7\'f1\'cd\'ea\'d5\'fb\'a3\'ac\'be\'e4\'d7\'d3\'d6\'f7\'ce\'bd\'b4\'ee\'c5\'e4\'ca\'c7\'b7\'f1\'d5\'fd\'c8\'b7\'a3\'ac\'b5\'a5\'b8\'b4\'ca\'fd\'a1\'a2\'b4\'fa\'b4\'ca\'a1\'a2\'bd\'e9\'b4\'ca\'a1\'a2\'b4\'f3\'d0\'a1\'d0\'b4\'ba\'cd\'b1\'ea\'b5\'e3\'ca\'c7\'b7\'f1\'d7\'bc\'c8\'b7\'a3\'ac\'ca\'c7\'b7\'f1\'d0\'b4\'b3\'f6\'c1\'cb\'cf\'b2\'bb\'b6\'b5\'c4\'c0\'ed\'d3\'c9\'a1\'a3\par \pard\plain\lang2052\f1\fs20\sa0\sb180\ql \'b8\'f8\'bc\'d2\'b3\'a4\'b5\'c4\'d7\'a2\'a3\'ba\'b1\'be\'be\'ed\'b8\'b2\'b8\'c7\'bb\'a6\'bd\'cc\'b0\'e6\'c8\'fd\'c4\'ea\'bc\'b6\'c9\'cf\'cf\'c2\'b2\'e1\'b3\'a3\'bc\'fb\'d7\'d6\'c4\'b8\'d3\'eb\'d3\'ef\'d2\'f4\'a3\'a8\'b3\'a4\'b6\'cc\'d4\'aa\'d2\'f4\'b1\'e6\'ce\'f6\'a1\'a2\'d7\'d6\'c4\'b8\'cb\'b3\'d0\'f2\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a2\'d6\'f7\'cc\'e2\'b4\'ca\'bb\'e3\'a3\'a8\'d2\'c2\'ce\'ef\'a1\'a2\'cc\'ec\'c6\'f8\'a1\'a2\'bc\'be\'bd\'da\'a1\'a2\'b6\'af\'ce\'ef\'a1\'a2\'d2\'fb\'ca\'b3\'a1\'a2\'ca\'b1\'bc\'e4\'a3\'a9\'a1\'a2\'b5\'a5\'b4\'ca\'c6\'b4\'d0\'b4\'d3\'eb\'d3\'ef\'be\'b3\'d1\'a1\'b4\'ca\'a1\'a2be\'b6\'af\'b4\'ca\'d3\'ebhave/has\'a1\'a2\'d2\'bb\'b0\'e3\'cf\'d6\'d4\'da\'ca\'b1\'a1\'a2can\'a1\'a2\'b4\'fa\'b4\'ca\'a1\'a2\'cc\'d8\'ca\'e2\'d2\'c9\'ce\'ca\'be\'e4\'a1\'a2\'c1\'ac\'b4\'ca\'b3\'c9\'be\'e4\'a1\'a2\'c7\'e9\'be\'b0\'b6\'d4\'bb\'b0\'a1\'a2\'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'a3\'a8\'d3\'ca\'bc\'fe\'a1\'a2\'bf\'ce\'b3\'cc\'b1\'ed\'a1\'a2\'bc\'db\'b8\'f1\'b1\'ed\'a1\'a2\'bb\'ee\'b6\'af\'ca\'b1\'bf\'cc\'b1\'ed\'a3\'a9\'ba\'cd\'d0\'b4\'d7\'f7\'a1\'a3\'d5\'eb\'b6\'d4\'c9\'cf\'d2\'bb\'b7\'dd\'b4\'ed\'cc\'e2\'bc\'af\'a3\'ba\'b5\'da\'d2\'bb\'b4\'f3\'cc\'e2\'d3\'c3\'b3\'c9\'b6\'d4\'b1\'c8\'bd\'cf\'ba\'cd\'d5\'d2\'d2\'ec\'c0\'e0\'d6\'d8\'b5\'e3\'c7\'bf\'bb\'af\'b3\'a4\'d4\'aa\'d2\'f4/\'b6\'cc\'d4\'aa\'d2\'f4\'a3\'a8he\'d3\'ebpen\'a1\'a2pupil\'d3\'ebsun\'a1\'a2duck\'b5\'c8\'a3\'a9\'a3\'bb\'b5\'da\'b6\'fe\'b4\'f3\'cc\'e2\'d3\'c3\'c3\'d5\'d3\'ef\'a1\'a2\'b2\'b9\'c8\'ab\'d7\'d6\'c4\'b8\'b5\'c8\'d0\'ce\'ca\'bd\'bc\'af\'d6\'d0\'b8\'b4\'cf\'d6\'d0\'b4\'b4\'ed\'b5\'c4dress\'a1\'a2gloves\'a1\'a2Thursday\'bc\'b0\'c6\'b4\'d0\'b4\'b2\'bb\'ce\'c8\'b5\'c4breakfast\'a1\'a2favourite\'a1\'a2vegetable\'a1\'a2beautiful\'a1\'a2grandmother\'a1\'a2weather\'b5\'c8\'b4\'ca\'a3\'bb\'b5\'da\'c8\'fd\'b4\'f3\'cc\'e2\'bc\'d3\'c8\'eb\'a1\'b0\'d5\'d2\'b4\'ed\'b2\'a2\'b8\'c4\'d5\'fd\'a1\'b1\'d7\'a8\'cf\'ee\'a3\'ac\'bc\'ec\'b2\'e9in/at/on\'ca\'b1\'bc\'e4\'bd\'e9\'b4\'ca\'ba\'cd\'b4\'fa\'b4\'ca\'d6\'f7\'b8\'f1/\'ce\'ef\'d6\'f7\'b4\'fa\'b4\'ca\'a3\'bb\'b5\'da\'cb\'c4\'b4\'f3\'cc\'e2\'d4\'da\'b9\'ba\'ce\'ef\'b6\'d4\'bb\'b0\'d6\'d0\'d4\'d9\'b4\'ce\'d1\'b5\'c1\'b7\'a1\'b0Which one do you like?\'a1\'b1\'a3\'bb\'b5\'da\'ce\'e5\'b4\'f3\'cc\'e2A\'a1\'a2B\'d3\'c3\'cf\'b8\'bd\'da\'c5\'d0\'b6\'cf\'cc\'e2\'ba\'cd\'bf\'ce\'b3\'cc\'b1\'ed\'cc\'e2\'a3\'ac\'d7\'a8\'c3\'c5\'d5\'eb\'b6\'d4\'c9\'cf\'d2\'bb\'b7\'dd\'b6\'c1\'b4\'ed\'c6\'f0\'b4\'b2\'ca\'b1\'bc\'e4\'a1\'a2\'ca\'fd\'b4\'ed\'bf\'ce\'ca\'b1\'a1\'a2\'c2\'a9\'bf\'b4\'c3\'bf\'d6\'dc\'b6\'bc\'d3\'d0\'d3\'ef\'ce\'c4\'bf\'ce\'b5\'c8\'ce\'ca\'cc\'e2\'c9\'e8\'bc\'c6\'a3\'bbC\'a1\'a2D\'c1\'bd\'d7\'e9\'b7\'c7\'c1\'ac\'d0\'f8\'d0\'d4\'ce\'c4\'b1\'be\'b0\'ef\'d6\'fa\'ba\'a2\'d7\'d3\'d1\'a7\'bb\'e1\'b4\'d3\'bc\'db\'b8\'f1\'b1\'ed\'ba\'cd\'ca\'b1\'bf\'cc\'b1\'ed\'d6\'d0\'cc\'e1\'c8\'a1\'d0\'c5\'cf\'a2\'b2\'a2\'d7\'f6\'bc\'f2\'b5\'a5\'bc\'c6\'cb\'e3\'c5\'d0\'b6\'cf\'a1\'a3\'d0\'b4\'d7\'f7\'cc\'e2\'c7\'eb\'d6\'d8\'b5\'e3\'bf\'b4\'be\'e4\'d7\'d3\'ca\'c7\'b7\'f1\'cd\'ea\'d5\'fb\'a1\'a2\'b4\'fa\'b4\'ca\'ba\'cd\'bd\'e9\'b4\'ca\'ca\'c7\'b7\'f1\'d5\'fd\'c8\'b7\'a1\'a3\'b1\'be\'be\'ed\'b2\'bb\'cf\'de\'b6\'a8\'ca\'b1\'bc\'e4\'ba\'cd\'b7\'d6\'ca\'fd\'a3\'ac\'bf\'c9\'b7\'d6\'b6\'ce\'cd\'ea\'b3\'c9\'a3\'ac\'d4\'c4\'b6\'c1\'cc\'e2\'b9\'c4\'c0\'f8\'bb\'d8\'b5\'bd\'ce\'c4\'d6\'d0\'c8\'a6\'b3\'f6\'d2\'c0\'be\'dd\'a1\'a3\par }